Arara Code: generic extension-owned blocking webview modal.

Why a patch: the public/proposed webview API has no blocking modal, CannotClose
capability, lifecycle veto or command admission hook. Reuse the native modal
editor and its existing focus/layout machinery instead of intercepting DOM keys
or reopening a closed tab. The extension supplies arara.modal.viewType and an
exact arara.modal.allowedCommands list; clearing the viewType releases the gate.
CannotClose prevents editor/modal dismissal. Closing the window stays possible;
the extension resumes its flow on the next launch.
No setup steps, provider names, business decisions or process execution here.
Touches: command service, webview editor input/service, native modal part/CSS.

